<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23900" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insomnĭum</span></b> ,
			ĭi, n.
		in-somnus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a dream</i> (mostly in plur.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> In
			sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illud haud ambigitur, qualicumque insomnio ipsi
					fratrique perniciem allatam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					11, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per insomnium dicere,</span>”
				<i>in a dream</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 7, 244</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ipsa insomnii verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 1, 3</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			In plur., <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun. 2, 1, 13</span></i> Umpfenbach;
				<i><span class="en">Tib.
				3, 4, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 896</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sil.
				10, 358</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11,
				102</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 12, 30, §
		118</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
